# Deployment checklist (one-time, technical)

For the person setting this up once. After this, the school administrator runs
everything from inside the app (see HANDOVER.md) and never touches these tools.

Target: **hosted** Supabase + a static host (Vercel/Netlify/Cloudflare Pages).
Free at one school's scale. ~30 minutes.

> Hosted vs local note: on **hosted** Supabase the `auth` schema, `auth.uid()`,
> and the `anon`/`authenticated`/`service_role` roles already exist. So you only
> apply the app schema + a small bootstrap here. The files
> `10-auth-helpers.sql`, `00-roles.sh`, and `30-grants.sql` from the local
> bundle are for self-hosting **only** — do not run them on hosted Supabase.

---

## 1. Create the Supabase project
- supabase.com → New project. Pick the nearest region. **Save the database
  password.**
- Project Settings → API. Copy: **Project URL**, **anon key**, **service_role
  key** (keep service_role secret — server only).

## 2. Apply the database
In the SQL editor, run, in order:
1. `schema_v3.2.sql`
2. `schema_v3.3_timetable.sql`
3. `schema_v3.4_stages.sql`

(These create the tables, RLS, functions, and timetable/stage features.)

## 3. Create the first admin
- Authentication → Users → **Add user**: email + password, tick *auto-confirm*.
  Copy the new user's UUID.
- SQL editor — create the school and the admin profile (replace the UUID):
  ```sql
  insert into schools (id, name, principal_name)
  values (gen_random_uuid(), 'Your School', 'Principal') returning id;
  -- use the returned school id below:
  insert into profiles (id, school_id, full_name, email, role, is_teaching)
  values ('<new-auth-user-uuid>', '<school-id>', 'School Admin',
          'admin@yourschool.example', 'admin', false);
  ```
- (Optional) add a grading scale — see the bootstrap block in `schema_v3.2.sql`.

## 4. Deploy the user-management function
The "Teachers & staff" screen calls this. `SUPABASE_URL` and
`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` are injected into Edge Functions automatically — no
secrets to set.
```bash
npm i -g supabase
supabase login
supabase link --project-ref <your-project-ref>
supabase functions deploy admin-users
```

## 5. Deploy the front-end
- Push the `school-admin` folder to a Git repo, then import it in **Vercel**
  (framework: Vite). Set environment variables:
  ```
  VITE_SUPABASE_URL = https://<project>.supabase.co
  VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = <anon key>
  ```
- Deploy. (Netlify/Cloudflare Pages work the same way: build `npm run build`,
  publish `dist`, set the two env vars.)
- Put the resulting URL into HANDOVER.md.

## 6. Test
- Open the site, sign in as the admin.
- **Teachers & staff → Add person** → add a test teacher. Sign in as them in a
  private window to confirm. Then disable/reset to confirm those work.

## 7. Strongly recommended
- Supabase → upgrade to **Pro (~$25/mo)** for automatic daily backups and no
  project pausing. Worth it for student records.
- Hand the school the Supabase + Vercel account credentials, stored safely.

---

## Notes / gotchas
- Email sending isn't required: admins set temporary passwords directly, so no
  SMTP setup is needed.
- The `admin-users` function is the only privileged path; the browser never
  holds the service-role key.
- This deployment uses the same app code as local — only the two env vars differ.
